OpenHSP for Debian/Ubuntu
=========================

The command-line hspcmp entry point is a wrapper around
/usr/lib/openhsp/hspcmp. It supplies the packaged common include directory and
runtime directory by default:

  --compath=/usr/lib/openhsp/common/
  --syspath=/usr/lib/openhsp/

Pass a later --compath or --syspath option if a project needs a custom tree.

GPIO support
------------

The Linux runtimes do not link GPIO backends directly. GPIO commands are
enabled only when an optional GPIO provider package is installed. Install
openhsp-gpio-gpiod for the Linux GPIO character device interface, or
openhsp-gpio-sysfs for the legacy /sys/class/gpio interface used by older
Raspberry Pi setups. This keeps the default openhsp package usable on systems
without GPIO hardware or libgpiod, while allowing GPIO users to add support
separately.
